0	182	Roxana Mînzatu (Romanian pronunciation: [roˈksana mɨnˈzatu]; born 1 April 1980) is a Romanian politician, local government official and manager of European Union projects in Romania.
183	301	In 2016, she was elected to the Romanian Chamber of Deputies and in 2019, was appointed as Minister of European Funds.
302	365	In 2024 she was elected as a Member of the European Parliament.
366	564	Since December 2024 she serves as Vice-President of the European Commission and Commissioner for Social Rights and Skills, Quality Jobs and Preparedness under the Second Von der Leyen Commission.



564	632	Early life and education
Mînzatu was born on 1 April 1980 in Brașov.
633	804	She obtained a BA in political science in 2002 from the University of Bucharest and an MA in European integration in 2005, from the Dimitrie Cantemir Christian University.
805	881	From 2004 to 2006, she was employed at the Ministry of European Integration.
882	999	She later worked as a manager and consultant for several projects, particularly those financed by the European Union.
1000	1069	Her activities also included running a non-profit business school.



1069	1181	Political career
Mînzatu became involved in local political activities within the Social Democratic Party (PSD).
1182	1259	She was a member of the Brasov district council (2004–2008, 2011–2012, 2016).
1260	1408	In 2015, she was appointed Secretary of State at the Ministry of European Funds, and then headed the National Agency for Public Procurement (ANAP).

1408	1597	In 2016, Mînzatu was elected to the Romanian Chamber of Deputies, where she became secretary of the Committee for Industries and Services and a member of the Committee for European Affairs.
